\ VOCABS.SEQ    ONLY ALSO vocabulary operators.         F-PC native port

\ CONTEXT is an array of #VOCS cells; the last one always holds ROOT.

CONTEXT DUP @ SWAP CELL+ !   ( Make FORTH also )

VOCABULARY ROOT   ROOT DEFINITIONS

: ALSO          ( -- )
                CONTEXT DUP CELL+ #VOCS 2- CELLS CMOVE>   ;

: ONLY          ( -- )
                ['] ROOT >BODY  CONTEXT #VOCS 1- CELLS 2DUP ERASE + !
                ROOT ;

: SEAL          ( -- )
                ' >BODY   CONTEXT #VOCS CELLS ERASE   CONTEXT !   ;

: PREVIOUS      ( -- )
                CONTEXT DUP CELL+ SWAP #VOCS 2- CELLS CMOVE
                CONTEXT #VOCS 2- CELLS + OFF   ;

: FORTH         ( --- ) FORTH ;
: DEFINITIONS   ( --- ) DEFINITIONS   ;

: ORDER         ( -- )
                CR ." Context: " CONTEXT #VOCS 0 DO DUP @ ?DUP
                IF  BODY> >NAME .ID THEN   CELL+ LOOP DROP
                CR ." Current: " CURRENT @ BODY> >NAME .ID  ;

: VOCS          ( -- )
                CR VOC-LINK @ BEGIN   DUP #THREADS CELLS -
                BODY> >NAME .ID ?CR @ DUP 0= UNTIL   DROP   ;

\ Native port: the VM's seed interpreter left primitive ONLY ALSO and
\ PREVIOUS headers in FORTH, which would shadow the ROOT words above
\ whenever FORTH is searched first. Point FORTH's names at ROOT's words.
' FORTH-VOC >IS @ >BODY CURRENT !       \ define in FORTH (the kernel's
                                        \ FORTH; ROOT's FORTH is a :),
                                        \ still searching ROOT first
' ONLY     ALIAS ONLY
' ALSO     ALIAS ALSO
' PREVIOUS ALIAS PREVIOUS

ONLY FORTH ALSO DEFINITIONS
VOCABULARY HIDDEN               \ Some vocabularies we will need.
VOCABULARY BUG

